WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.189
Week 36: Integrated Field Capstone. manage an unfamiliar situation brief and persuade reflect on strengths and a maintenance plan

2
00:00:09.189 --> 00:00:19.103
Cultural lens. Intercultural competence means observing, asking, adapting, and avoiding claims that one community represents all speakers.

3
00:00:19.103 --> 00:00:31.174
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:31.174 --> 00:00:43.032
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:43.032 --> 00:00:52.031
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:52.031 --> 00:01:25.265
Model language. La competencia intercultural exige observar primero. — Intercultural competence requires observing first. También exige preguntar sin asumir. — It also requires asking without assuming. Ajustarse a cada contexto es clave. — Adjusting to each context is key. Ninguna persona representa a todas las demás. — No single person represents everyone else. El respeto mutuo evita la generalización. — Mutual respect avoids generalization.

7
00:01:25.265 --> 00:01:35.185
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
